WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.218
Both balls travel the same distance in the same time.

2
00:00:02.218 --> 00:00:05.063
The top one moves at one constant speed, which feels like a machine.

3
00:00:05.063 --> 00:00:07.741
The bottom one eases: it starts gently, speeds up, then settles.

4
00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.000
That small difference is what makes motion feel alive.

5
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.218
Spacing is where the ball sits from one moment to the next.

6
00:00:13.218 --> 00:00:16.273
Dots close together mean slow, dots far apart mean fast.

7
00:00:16.273 --> 00:00:19.000
Easing is just spacing that changes along the way.

8
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.602
Timing is how long the move takes.

9
00:00:20.602 --> 00:00:22.251
A quarter of a second feels snappy.

10
00:00:22.251 --> 00:00:24.372
Around two thirds of a second feels friendly.

11
00:00:24.372 --> 00:00:26.539
Over a second and a half feels heavy and slow.

12
00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:28.000
Same move, three personalities.

13
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Here is your first experiment.

14
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.163
Pick one simple move.

15
00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:31.845
Add easing.

16
00:00:31.845 --> 00:00:33.705
Try three different durations.

17
00:00:33.705 --> 00:00:36.000
Keep the one that feels right to you.
